Advantages and Disadvantages of this, hence what came next
==========================================================

Advantages
----------
1. Prevents unauthorized switches.
2. Protects STP topology.
3. Prevents rogue trunk creation.
4. Reduces attack surface.
5. Improves network security.
6. Prevents accidental switch connections.
7. Helps maintain network stability.

Disadvantages
-------------
1. Requires proper port configuration.
2. Legitimate switch connections may be blocked.
3. Additional management overhead.
4. Multiple security features must be combined.
5. Not a complete endpoint authentication solution.

Hence what came next
--------------------
Even after preventing rogue switches, administrators needed a way to detect actual link communication failures.

A cable may appear UP while traffic passes only in one direction.

This led to:

UDLD (Unidirectional Link Detection)

which detects one-way communication failures and disables affected links.

One-Shot Configuration
======================

Access Port Hardening

Switch(config)# interface range fa0/1-24
Switch(config-if-range)# switchport mode access
Switch(config-if-range)# switchport nonegotiate


Enable PortFast

Switch(config-if-range)# spanning-tree portfast


Enable BPDU Guard

Switch(config-if-range)# spanning-tree bpduguard enable


Enable Port Security

Switch(config-if-range)# switchport port-security
Switch(config-if-range)# switchport port-security maximum 1
Switch(config-if-range)# switchport port-security violation shutdown
Switch(config-if-range)# switchport port-security mac-address sticky

Verification
============

show spanning-tree summary

show port-security

show interfaces status

show errdisable recovery

